# Meet household needs

<p id="wg-001">Before you write, know who in the home needs this and what they are trying to do.</p>

Include only what that task needs. A card hint, for example, gives only what someone needs to finish the task in front of them.

Written this way, your content is:

- specific
- informative
- clear and to the point

A dashboard has done its job when someone glances at it, acts and gets on with their day without stopping to think.

<p id="wg-002">Change only the words Civica owns. Keep <a href="clear-language.html#wg-021">native Home Assistant labels, translations and names people typed</a> exactly as they are.</p>

Help text that Civica owns can change. A name someone chose, such as “Nain’s lamp”, stays as they typed it. A native label, such as a translated “Notifications”, stays as Home Assistant shows it.

Improve “Choose a light to add to this room” if it is unclear, but do not rename “Nain’s lamp” or “Notifications” to make a sentence read better.
